  {
  "slug": "income-tax-return-documents-individual-business-checklist",
  "category": "Income Tax",
  "title": "Income Tax Return Documents Checklist for Individuals and Small Businesses",
  "excerpt": "Organise salary, bank interest, capital gains, business books, deductions and tax-payment records before preparing an income-tax return.",
  "metaTitle": "ITR Filing Documents Checklist for Individuals & Businesses",
  "metaDescription": "A practical ITR checklist covering salary, bank interest, capital gains, business income, deductions and tax payments for Indian taxpayers.",
  "content": "Preparing an income-tax return begins with identifying the correct taxpayer profile and return form. A salary-only return, a return with capital gains and a business return require different records. Do not select a form only because it was used in the previous year; check the current assessment-year instructions and all income sources.\\n\\n## 1. Identity and filing history\\nKeep PAN, bank account information, contact details and previous-year ITR acknowledgement available. Review earlier computations, outstanding demands, refund adjustments and notices. Confirm the assessment year and financial year covered by the records.\\n\\n## 2. Salary and pension\\nCollect Form 16 from every employer, salary slips where needed, allowance and perquisite details, and pension statements. If there were multiple employers, combine the information and check that salary and TDS are not duplicated or omitted.\\n\\n## 3. Interest, dividends and investments\\nReview savings and deposit interest certificates, bank statements, dividend statements and other income records. Compare information with AIS and Form 26AS, investigate differences and retain explanations for timing or reporting variations.\\n\\n## 4. Capital gains\\nFor shares and mutual funds, collect broker capital-gains statements, acquisition dates and cost information. For property, retain purchase and sale deeds, improvement-cost evidence, transfer expenses and any valuation or reinvestment documents relevant to a claim. Do not estimate cost or holding period without evidence.\\n\\n## 5. Business and professional income\\nProprietors and professionals should organise sales registers, expense ledgers, bank statements, invoices, loan interest, asset purchases, depreciation details and prior-year financial statements. Marketplace sellers should separately retain order, refund, fee, settlement and TCS reports so gross sales are not confused with net bank credits.\\n\\n## 6. Deductions and tax payments\\nKeep proof for deductions or exemptions actually claimed, eligible donations, insurance or housing-loan records where relevant, advance-tax challans and self-assessment tax challans. A document does not automatically make an expense deductible; eligibility and limits depend on the tax regime and assessment year.\\n\\n## 7. Reconcile before submission\\nCompare salary TDS, other TDS, TCS, advance tax and self-assessment tax with Form 26AS and the computation. Review AIS entries and explain material differences. Check bank validation and refund details before submitting.\\n\\n## Final review checklist\\n- Confirm taxpayer status, residential status and income sources.\\n- Select the return form using current official instructions.\\n- Reconcile books, AIS, Form 26AS and tax challans.\\n- Verify deductions, exemptions and regime selection.\\n- Review bank details, tax payable and refund.\\n- Save the filed return and verification confirmation.\\n\\n## How FileFast can help\\nFileFast Global can help organise ITR records, reconcile tax information, prepare the computation and assist with return filing for the agreed scope. Complex capital gains, foreign assets, notices, audit matters or specialist opinions may require additional review. The taxpayer must verify the final return and complete e-verification within the applicable time.\\n\\nOfficial reference: https://www.incometax.gov.in/"
}
